1
00:00:12,128 --> 00:00:14,587
(pain shriek)

2
00:00:20,254 --> 00:00:21,338
[Mahito] Ahh!

3
00:00:21,421 --> 00:00:23,254
There you are!

4
00:00:23,338 --> 00:00:25,338
-(laughs)
-Hm?

5
00:00:25,421 --> 00:00:28,546
Jougo!

6
00:00:28,629 --> 00:00:31,088
(laughs)

7
00:00:31,171 --> 00:00:33,922
(unhappy grumble)

8
00:00:34,006 --> 00:00:35,486
I see you have most
of your body back.

9
00:00:37,089 --> 00:00:39,922
Yeah, this is a good
place to rejuvenate.

10
00:00:40,006 --> 00:00:41,315
Humans don't come
anywhere near it.

11
00:00:41,339 --> 00:00:44,422
[Mahito] Not having a
body really sucks, huh?

12
00:00:45,631 --> 00:00:47,214
It makes self-preservation
so difficult.

13
00:00:47,298 --> 00:00:49,548
Mahito.

14
00:00:49,631 --> 00:00:52,590
You should know, you're
awfully worn down yourself.

15
00:00:52,673 --> 00:00:53,798
Oh, you can tell?

16
00:00:53,882 --> 00:00:57,757
It turns out Sukuna and his
vessel are my natural enemies.

17
00:00:58,340 --> 00:01:00,341
I started this whole game

18
00:01:00,424 --> 00:01:02,632
because I happened
to acquire a new toy.

19
00:01:03,299 --> 00:01:08,050
It was great at first but
then it didn't work out.

20
00:01:08,132 --> 00:01:09,758
Should've used a hostage.

21
00:01:09,841 --> 00:01:12,925
Then I could've forced
him into a pact, am I right?

22
00:01:13,009 --> 00:01:14,759
Hand your body over to Sukuna,

23
00:01:14,842 --> 00:01:17,133
if you don't want to
see this dude killed!

24
00:01:17,216 --> 00:01:19,051
(aggravated growl)

25
00:01:19,133 --> 00:01:21,383
You failed, because
pacts are only ever placed

26
00:01:21,467 --> 00:01:23,342
by oneself on oneself.

27
00:01:23,425 --> 00:01:26,593
It's not easy to forge
pacts with others,

28
00:01:26,676 --> 00:01:28,593
because of
intervention from others.

29
00:01:30,052 --> 00:01:31,634
[Mahito] Maybe I
should have just given

30
00:01:31,718 --> 00:01:32,426
that thing a lethal wound,

31
00:01:32,509 --> 00:01:35,052
instead of transfiguring it.

32
00:01:35,551 --> 00:01:37,634
Then Sukuna might
have been able to heal it

33
00:01:37,718 --> 00:01:39,594
with his reverse
cursed technique.

34
00:01:40,552 --> 00:01:42,802
Don't forget your place.

35
00:01:42,886 --> 00:01:43,886
Foolish puppet.

36
00:01:44,344 --> 00:01:47,594
No, not with that personality.

37
00:01:47,677 --> 00:01:49,886
I think he would have
refused either way.

38
00:01:51,887 --> 00:01:52,970
Jougo?

39
00:01:53,054 --> 00:01:54,636
Touching Sukuna made me realize

40
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:57,887
that we should probably
proceed with Getou's plan, for now.

41
00:01:58,386 --> 00:02:00,261
Sukuna is that valuable.

42
00:02:00,345 --> 00:02:02,261
(suspicious grumble)

43
00:02:03,511 --> 00:02:06,137
You mean gather all the fingers

44
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:08,055
and offer them to Sukuna, huh?

45
00:02:09,554 --> 00:02:13,721
Even if that means we all get
wiped out in the process, eh?

46
00:02:14,721 --> 00:02:15,721
Very well then.

47
00:02:17,471 --> 00:02:19,889
I sure don't intend to
be the one left laughing

48
00:02:19,972 --> 00:02:22,889
like a lunatic in the
wasteland a century from now.

49
00:02:22,972 --> 00:02:25,472
As long as curses exist as
people that's all that matters.

50
00:02:25,555 --> 00:02:27,305
Oh!

51
00:02:27,388 --> 00:02:29,138
You understand exactly!

52
00:02:29,221 --> 00:02:31,015
Good, then first we
need to go retrieve

53
00:02:31,098 --> 00:02:32,282
the six fingers
from Jujutsu Tech.

54
00:02:32,306 --> 00:02:35,139
Do we have to?

55
00:02:35,222 --> 00:02:36,015
I thought the sorcerers

56
00:02:36,098 --> 00:02:37,407
were only keeping
Yuuji Itadori around

57
00:02:37,431 --> 00:02:40,681
so that he can swallow
Sukuna's fingers.

58
00:02:40,765 --> 00:02:42,365
If we leave him alone
he'll still eat them.

59
00:02:42,389 --> 00:02:45,140
The higher-ups at Jujutsu Tech

60
00:02:45,223 --> 00:02:46,325
are still trying to calculate

61
00:02:46,349 --> 00:02:49,182
Yuuji Itadori's
strength as a vessel.

62
00:02:49,265 --> 00:02:52,099
They want to see just how
many fingers he can take.

63
00:02:52,182 --> 00:02:53,724
They want to
gather all the fingers

64
00:02:53,807 --> 00:02:55,557
and then have him consume them.

65
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:57,516
With just one exception.

66
00:02:57,600 --> 00:02:58,516
"Exception"

67
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:01,266
I want him to eat them all, now!

68
00:03:01,350 --> 00:03:03,266
But we can't just wait around.

69
00:03:03,350 --> 00:03:06,558
Worst case, there's the
chance they could decide

70
00:03:06,641 --> 00:03:09,183
to eliminate Yuuji Itadori.

71
00:03:09,266 --> 00:03:12,060
So into the tiger's
den we go, huh?

72
00:03:12,142 --> 00:03:14,559
Then just how do you
think we oughta proceed?

73
00:03:14,642 --> 00:03:15,684
Already started.

74
00:03:16,684 --> 00:03:19,060
My first move was
allowing Jujutsu Tech

75
00:03:19,142 --> 00:03:20,517
to retrieve the fingers we had.

76
00:03:24,643 --> 00:03:27,769
(opening theme music)

77
00:04:45,274 --> 00:04:46,399
"Jujutsu Kaisen"

78
00:04:55,566 --> 00:04:57,026
"Episode 14:

79
00:04:57,109 --> 00:04:59,317
"Kyoto Sister School Exchange
Event - Group Battle 0-"

80
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:00,525
Nanami!

81
00:05:00,609 --> 00:05:04,859
Come on, would you
say something interesting!

82
00:05:04,942 --> 00:05:06,192
(light exasperated grunt)

83
00:05:06,275 --> 00:05:07,192
Okay!

84
00:05:07,275 --> 00:05:08,984
I've got it! Yeah!

85
00:05:09,068 --> 00:05:10,586
We'll record us playing
catch with a stale rice ball!

86
00:05:10,610 --> 00:05:13,860
While discussing
economic policies!

87
00:05:13,943 --> 00:05:16,234
Then we'll post a
video and go trolling!

88
00:05:18,151 --> 00:05:19,485
You can enjoy that on your own.

89
00:05:19,568 --> 00:05:22,319
What kind of idea is that?

90
00:05:22,402 --> 00:05:23,486
A drinking game then!

91
00:05:23,569 --> 00:05:26,319
Name all the things you
like about Satoru Gojou!

92
00:05:26,402 --> 00:05:27,611
See who names the most!

93
00:05:27,694 --> 00:05:28,861
My turn.

94
00:05:28,944 --> 00:05:29,944
Everything!

95
00:05:31,402 --> 00:05:33,527
You just keep on
thinking that way.

96
00:05:34,194 --> 00:05:35,695
It's totally idiotic,

97
00:05:35,779 --> 00:05:38,695
but Itadori needs that
kind of idiocy right now.

98
00:05:39,987 --> 00:05:41,787
You'll be sent out on
more difficult missions.

99
00:05:43,987 --> 00:05:44,862
To be honest though,

100
00:05:44,945 --> 00:05:47,695
that wasn't the kind
of difficult I meant.

101
00:05:48,780 --> 00:05:49,863
Nanami?

102
00:05:49,946 --> 00:05:51,505
Does Yuuji know about that
finger in Junpei Yoshino's--

103
00:05:51,529 --> 00:05:54,072
I haven't told him.

104
00:05:54,154 --> 00:05:58,072
Knowing Yuuji, he'd just
feel unnecessarily responsible.

105
00:05:58,154 --> 00:06:00,363
I'm glad I left you
in charge of him.

106
00:06:00,446 --> 00:06:01,446
So, where is it now?

107
00:06:03,155 --> 00:06:04,590
I submitted it to the
higher-ups, of course.

108
00:06:04,614 --> 00:06:06,864
If I gave it to you,

109
00:06:06,947 --> 00:06:08,864
you would've already
fed it to Itadori.

110
00:06:08,947 --> 00:06:09,864
Ouch.

111
00:06:09,947 --> 00:06:10,989
But...

112
00:06:11,073 --> 00:06:14,364
Are you really sure that
it's safe to bring him back?

113
00:06:14,447 --> 00:06:17,365
If they find out he's alive
at the exchange event,

114
00:06:17,448 --> 00:06:19,573
won't the higher-ups
just target him again?

115
00:06:19,656 --> 00:06:21,615
Even if they do
Yuuji will be fine now.

116
00:06:21,698 --> 00:06:24,740
You know that better
than anyone, don't you?

117
00:06:25,656 --> 00:06:26,573
(sigh)

118
00:06:26,656 --> 00:06:27,948
Hey! Gojou!

119
00:06:28,032 --> 00:06:31,116
(laugh)

120
00:06:31,199 --> 00:06:32,949
Oh, Nanami's here too!

121
00:06:33,033 --> 00:06:34,075
Well come on guys!

122
00:06:34,157 --> 00:06:35,949
Let's hurry up, I
wanna go see everyone!

123
00:06:36,033 --> 00:06:37,574
I can't wait!

124
00:06:37,657 --> 00:06:39,407
Can't wait!

125
00:06:39,491 --> 00:06:39,824
It's so exciting!

126
00:06:39,908 --> 00:06:40,532
I'm so pumped!

127
00:06:40,616 --> 00:06:43,575
Yuuji? What are you thinking?

128
00:06:43,658 --> 00:06:44,742
After all this time,

129
00:06:44,825 --> 00:06:46,658
you can just show up
like nothing happened?

130
00:06:46,742 --> 00:06:48,200
(shock gasp) I can't?

131
00:06:49,492 --> 00:06:50,950
Even among sorcerers it's rare

132
00:06:51,034 --> 00:06:53,158
to essentially come
back from the dead

133
00:06:53,241 --> 00:06:55,409
after being gone for
like two whole months.

134
00:06:55,493 --> 00:06:57,534
So we have to
make it a surprise!

135
00:06:57,618 --> 00:07:00,159
A surprise, how?

136
00:07:00,242 --> 00:07:01,677
[Gojou] You just
leave all that to me!

137
00:07:01,701 --> 00:07:02,701
Huh?

138
00:07:04,701 --> 00:07:06,618
[Gojou] The first-years will be

139
00:07:06,701 --> 00:07:08,219
crying and laughing
from happiness and shock.

140
00:07:08,243 --> 00:07:09,036
I'm so happy! I'm so happy!

141
00:07:09,119 --> 00:07:11,160
[Gojou] The second-years
and Kyoto students

142
00:07:11,243 --> 00:07:12,160
will cry with them,

143
00:07:12,243 --> 00:07:13,827
and someone will
choke up and vomit!

144
00:07:13,911 --> 00:07:14,911
(vomiting)

145
00:07:14,952 --> 00:07:19,202
And in the end, it'll even
solve global warming!

146
00:07:19,285 --> 00:07:20,285
[] Cool!

147
00:07:22,203 --> 00:07:23,120
So cool!

148
00:07:23,203 --> 00:07:24,995
So, what's my
job in this, tell me!

149
00:07:25,079 --> 00:07:25,912
What do I have to do here?

150
00:07:25,995 --> 00:07:28,453
You don't have to
do anything, Yuuji.

151
00:07:28,536 --> 00:07:31,328
You just do exactly as I
say and go with the flow!

152
00:07:31,411 --> 00:07:32,411
Hey I can do that!

153
00:07:32,495 --> 00:07:33,370
I can go with the flow!

154
00:07:33,453 --> 00:07:35,454
[Nanami] It'll be enough
of a surprise for them

155
00:07:35,537 --> 00:07:37,454
just to see he's alive.

156
00:07:37,537 --> 00:07:38,329
Hey!

157
00:07:38,412 --> 00:07:41,245
Why are you guys
all empty-handed?

158
00:07:41,329 --> 00:07:42,412
[All] Hm?

159
00:07:42,496 --> 00:07:44,746
Where do you think you're
going with all that luggage?

160
00:07:44,829 --> 00:07:45,829
Wait a sec.

161
00:07:45,871 --> 00:07:47,872
Aren't we all traveling today?

162
00:07:47,955 --> 00:07:51,246
For the exchange event with
our sister school in Kyoto?

163
00:07:51,330 --> 00:07:52,663
Yes it's an exchange event

164
00:07:52,747 --> 00:07:53,890
with our sister school in Kyoto.

165
00:07:53,914 --> 00:07:55,705
Here in Tokyo.

166
00:07:55,789 --> 00:07:57,747
No freaking way!

167
00:07:58,747 --> 00:08:02,498
That explains why she hasn't
been making any sense lately.

168
00:08:02,581 --> 00:08:02,790
No doubt.

169
00:08:02,873 --> 00:08:04,664
Salmon.

170
00:08:04,748 --> 00:08:06,748
The previous year's
winner always hosts it.

171
00:08:06,831 --> 00:08:08,998
So why'd you have
to go and win it?

172
00:08:09,082 --> 00:08:10,724
It wasn't us! We weren't
even in it last year!

173
00:08:10,748 --> 00:08:13,623
They just put in Yuuta so
the numbers would match up!

174
00:08:13,706 --> 00:08:17,041
Yeah 'cause that was
before Rika got freed.

175
00:08:17,124 --> 00:08:19,041
Apparently, it was
an overwhelming win,

176
00:08:19,124 --> 00:08:22,290
but I didn't get to see it
since it was held in Kyoto.

177
00:08:22,374 --> 00:08:24,415
I'll never forgive
you Yuuta Okkotsu!

178
00:08:24,499 --> 00:08:26,707
Even though in fact,
I've never met you!

179
00:08:26,791 --> 00:08:28,084
Misdirected rage.

180
00:08:28,166 --> 00:08:29,416
-Salmon.
-Hm?

181
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,541
Hey.

182
00:08:34,625 --> 00:08:35,750
Here they come.

183
00:08:35,833 --> 00:08:37,708
Oh damn.

184
00:08:37,792 --> 00:08:40,626
The whole Tokyo
crowd all together, huh?

185
00:08:41,793 --> 00:08:45,250
You actually came to greet us?

186
00:08:45,334 --> 00:08:46,459
So amateur.

187
00:08:46,542 --> 00:08:47,810
"Jujutsu Tech, Kyoto
Second-Year Zenin Mai"

188
00:08:47,834 --> 00:08:50,709
I don't see Okkotsu though.

189
00:08:50,793 --> 00:08:53,085
"Jujutsu Tech, Kyoto
Third-Year Toudou Aoi"

190
00:08:53,167 --> 00:08:55,877
Oh shut your mouth already
and hand over the cake box.

191
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:58,418
And the yatsuhashi,
noodles and cookies.

192
00:08:58,502 --> 00:08:59,418
Salmon.

193
00:08:59,502 --> 00:09:01,251
[Aoi] What, are you guys hungry?

194
00:09:01,335 --> 00:09:03,293
Whoa, who is that first year?

195
00:09:03,377 --> 00:09:04,377
Badass.

196
00:09:04,418 --> 00:09:06,586
"Jujutsu Tech, Kyoto
Third-Year Nishimiya Momo"

197
00:09:06,669 --> 00:09:08,128
Never mind Okkotsu's absence,

198
00:09:08,211 --> 00:09:10,294
isn't fielding two
first-years a major handicap?

199
00:09:10,378 --> 00:09:12,128
[Nobara] Oh, it's
a freaking robot!

200
00:09:12,211 --> 00:09:13,045
"Jujutsu Tech, Kyoto
Second-Year Ultimate Mechamaru"

201
00:09:13,128 --> 00:09:16,586
With sorcerers,
physical age is irrelevant.

202
00:09:16,669 --> 00:09:18,669
"Jujutsu Tech, Kyoto
Third-Year Kamo Noritoshi"

203
00:09:18,753 --> 00:09:19,879
Especially with him.

204
00:09:19,962 --> 00:09:22,921
Fushiguro's from the Zenin
bloodline, but he's talented.

205
00:09:23,004 --> 00:09:25,921
More so even than
the head of the clan.

206
00:09:26,004 --> 00:09:27,004
(miffed grunt)

207
00:09:27,046 --> 00:09:28,295
Comment?

208
00:09:28,379 --> 00:09:29,295
Not here.

209
00:09:29,379 --> 00:09:30,629
Now now, you two!

210
00:09:30,712 --> 00:09:32,295
Save all that for
the event okay?

211
00:09:32,379 --> 00:09:34,140
"Jujutsu Tech, Kyoto
Second-Year Miwa Kasumi"

212
00:09:36,171 --> 00:09:37,981
Okay now, let's not fight
amongst ourselves alright?

213
00:09:38,005 --> 00:09:39,671
My goodness, these children.

214
00:09:39,755 --> 00:09:40,981
"Jujutsu Tech,
Semi-First-Grade Sorcerer

215
00:09:41,005 --> 00:09:42,963
"Kyoto School
Leader Iori Utahime"

216
00:09:43,047 --> 00:09:44,047
Now...

217
00:09:44,089 --> 00:09:44,838
Where's that idiot?

218
00:09:44,922 --> 00:09:47,006
Satoru's running late.

219
00:09:47,090 --> 00:09:48,964
As if that idiot ever
shows up on time.

220
00:09:49,048 --> 00:09:52,881
No one said idiot
specifically referred to Gojou.

221
00:09:52,964 --> 00:09:53,964
[All] Hm?

222
00:09:56,798 --> 00:09:57,964
Sorry for the wait!

223
00:09:58,048 --> 00:09:58,964
Hmph.

224
00:09:59,048 --> 00:10:02,423
-Satoru Gojou!
-Satoru Gojou!

225
00:10:02,507 --> 00:10:04,632
Glad to see everyone
all gathered together!

226
00:10:04,715 --> 00:10:06,858
I'm just getting back from a
big ol' business trip overseas!

227
00:10:06,882 --> 00:10:10,173
So now it's time to
hand out the souvenirs!

228
00:10:10,256 --> 00:10:12,007
This is sudden.

229
00:10:12,091 --> 00:10:13,549
Sure it's not jet lag?

230
00:10:13,633 --> 00:10:14,466
'Kay, everybody from Kyoto

231
00:10:14,549 --> 00:10:17,174
gets this tribal
protective charm doll.

232
00:10:17,257 --> 00:10:18,633
Except you Utahime.

233
00:10:18,716 --> 00:10:19,633
I don't want one!

234
00:10:19,716 --> 00:10:22,341
And now, for all of you
Tokyo peeps I have this!

235
00:10:22,424 --> 00:10:23,424
Ta-da!

236
00:10:23,800 --> 00:10:26,842
It's creepy when
adults get all excited.

237
00:10:29,967 --> 00:10:30,884
Hey!

238
00:10:30,967 --> 00:10:31,967
Opapi!

239
00:10:32,967 --> 00:10:36,425
It's your long-dead
friend Yuuji!

240
00:10:36,509 --> 00:10:39,010
(grossed-out horror gasp reax)

241
00:10:39,094 --> 00:10:41,385
Hey!

242
00:10:41,468 --> 00:10:42,551
What the hell?

243
00:10:42,635 --> 00:10:44,094
What kind of reaction is this?

244
00:10:44,176 --> 00:10:46,343
They don't seem
happy to see me at all!

245
00:10:47,135 --> 00:10:49,052
N-No way...

246
00:10:49,135 --> 00:10:50,593
Alrighty then.

247
00:10:50,676 --> 00:10:54,552
Everyone from Kyoto, this is
Sukuna's vessel, Yuuji Itadori!

248
00:10:54,636 --> 00:10:55,552
W-What?

249
00:10:55,636 --> 00:10:56,945
The Kyoto guys
aren't impressed either!

250
00:10:56,969 --> 00:10:58,969
They're all too absorbed
in their little souvenirs!

251
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:03,386
Sukuna's vessel lives?

252
00:11:03,469 --> 00:11:05,678
Just who is behind this outrage?

253
00:11:05,762 --> 00:11:07,072
"Jujutsu Tech, Kyoto School
Principal Gakuganji Yoshinobu"

254
00:11:07,096 --> 00:11:08,096
Huh?

255
00:11:08,137 --> 00:11:10,887
Oh Principal Gakuganji!

256
00:11:10,970 --> 00:11:12,970
Thank goodness you're all right.

257
00:11:13,054 --> 00:11:15,595
I was worried when you saw him

258
00:11:15,678 --> 00:11:17,720
that you might just
keel right over dead.

259
00:11:17,804 --> 00:11:19,221
You know, from the shock.

260
00:11:20,513 --> 00:11:22,596
You insolent damn brat!

261
00:11:22,679 --> 00:11:25,429
(mocking laughter)

262
00:11:27,013 --> 00:11:27,930
Hey.

263
00:11:28,013 --> 00:11:30,097
Uh, yeah?

264
00:11:30,179 --> 00:11:31,972
You got something
you wanna say to us?

265
00:11:32,056 --> 00:11:33,430
Uh...

266
00:11:33,514 --> 00:11:33,931
(squirming)

267
00:11:34,014 --> 00:11:37,722
(fuming)

268
00:11:37,806 --> 00:11:40,263
I'm sorry that I didn't tell you

269
00:11:40,347 --> 00:11:42,472
I was still alive all this time?

270
00:11:42,555 --> 00:11:43,806
"Itadori Rejoins"

271
00:11:47,973 --> 00:11:49,348
"Jujutsu Kaisen"

272
00:11:53,723 --> 00:11:55,640
"Jujutsu Kaisen"

273
00:11:55,723 --> 00:11:56,640
"Jujutsu Technical High School

274
00:11:56,723 --> 00:11:59,516
"Tokyo-Kyoto Sister
School Exchange Event"

275
00:11:59,599 --> 00:12:02,265
The Tokyo-Kyoto Sister
School Exchange Event

276
00:12:02,349 --> 00:12:04,641
will be held over two days.

277
00:12:04,724 --> 00:12:07,933
The first day is a group
battle: Exorcism Race!

278
00:12:10,724 --> 00:12:12,975
The Wacky Cursed
Spirit Exorcism Race!

279
00:12:16,017 --> 00:12:17,350
The rules are simple.

280
00:12:17,934 --> 00:12:21,475
The first team to exorcise
the second-grade cursed spirit

281
00:12:21,558 --> 00:12:24,643
released in the
designated area wins.

282
00:12:24,726 --> 00:12:25,994
Several third-grade
and lower cursed spirits

283
00:12:26,018 --> 00:12:29,643
will be released into the
designated area as well.

284
00:12:29,726 --> 00:12:31,078
If a winner is not
decided by sundown

285
00:12:31,102 --> 00:12:34,018
then the team that
exorcises the most wins.

286
00:12:34,102 --> 00:12:36,976
There are absolutely
no other rules.

287
00:12:37,060 --> 00:12:40,685
Of course, you're welcome
to sabotage the others.

288
00:12:40,769 --> 00:12:41,953
But remember, you're
all on the same side

289
00:12:41,977 --> 00:12:44,811
in the fight against the curses.

290
00:12:44,894 --> 00:12:46,310
This exchange
event will allow you

291
00:12:46,394 --> 00:12:48,352
to learn about yourselves,
and your comrades,

292
00:12:48,435 --> 00:12:49,435
through competition.

293
00:12:51,269 --> 00:12:53,895
Be certain at all times not
to kill other competitors

294
00:12:53,978 --> 00:12:57,353
or needlessly injure
them beyond recovery.

295
00:12:57,436 --> 00:12:58,728
(snickering)

296
00:12:58,812 --> 00:13:00,145
That's it!

297
00:13:00,228 --> 00:13:02,388
You're all dismissed until
the event commences at noon!

298
00:13:06,146 --> 00:13:06,938
"Tokyo Side Meeting"

299
00:13:07,021 --> 00:13:09,562
Uhh, guys?

300
00:13:09,646 --> 00:13:12,771
Depending on how you
look at the situation here,

301
00:13:12,854 --> 00:13:15,105
what you're doing could be
considered extreme bullying.

302
00:13:15,187 --> 00:13:16,105
Shut up.

303
00:13:16,187 --> 00:13:17,563
I think you've said enough.

304
00:13:17,647 --> 00:13:18,188
Now now...

305
00:13:18,271 --> 00:13:20,064
You heard his explanation.

306
00:13:20,147 --> 00:13:22,855
We should cut him some slack.

307
00:13:22,939 --> 00:13:24,397
A talking panda?

308
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:26,022
Salmon salmon.

309
00:13:26,106 --> 00:13:27,355
Say what?

310
00:13:27,438 --> 00:13:29,064
Inumaki is a cursed-speech user.

311
00:13:29,147 --> 00:13:33,065
His speech amplifies the
power and compulsion of words.

312
00:13:33,148 --> 00:13:36,065
He limits his vocabulary
to keep others safe.

313
00:13:36,148 --> 00:13:39,606
So if he told someone
to go die they'd do it?

314
00:13:39,689 --> 00:13:40,314
Awesome.

315
00:13:40,398 --> 00:13:43,107
It's nothing quite that simple.

316
00:13:43,189 --> 00:13:46,357
It always varies, depending
on the opponent's strengths.

317
00:13:46,440 --> 00:13:49,732
Using powerful words can
produce massive feedback.

318
00:13:49,816 --> 00:13:52,399
Worst case it can
affect him as well.

319
00:13:52,482 --> 00:13:54,000
Limiting his vocabulary
is a way for Toge

320
00:13:54,024 --> 00:13:56,440
to protect himself and others.

321
00:13:56,524 --> 00:13:57,109
Ahh...

322
00:13:57,191 --> 00:13:59,067
So, how is it you can speak?

323
00:13:59,150 --> 00:14:01,691
Are you a new breed of panda?

324
00:14:01,775 --> 00:14:04,274
Stop being so nosy about
everyone else's techniques!

325
00:14:04,358 --> 00:14:05,274
It's fine.

326
00:14:05,358 --> 00:14:08,400
Toge's ability's no big secret.

327
00:14:08,483 --> 00:14:09,900
More importantly, Yuuji...

328
00:14:09,984 --> 00:14:10,442
Huh?

329
00:14:10,526 --> 00:14:12,609
Hand over my blade!

330
00:14:13,943 --> 00:14:16,901
You borrowed Slaughter
Demon from Satoru, right?

331
00:14:16,984 --> 00:14:17,984
Uh oh...

332
00:14:21,359 --> 00:14:22,068
Gimme that.

333
00:14:22,151 --> 00:14:23,152
Here you go!

334
00:14:25,193 --> 00:14:26,193
I uhh...

335
00:14:28,485 --> 00:14:29,402
You jerks!

336
00:14:29,485 --> 00:14:31,777
(fright, trembling)

337
00:14:31,860 --> 00:14:32,902
Gojou has it.

338
00:14:33,860 --> 00:14:35,652
Last I saw it.

339
00:14:35,735 --> 00:14:37,945
The blindfolded dumbass!

340
00:14:38,028 --> 00:14:39,444
Hmm...

341
00:14:39,528 --> 00:14:41,112
(alarmed inhale)

342
00:14:41,194 --> 00:14:43,820
That was disgusting.

343
00:14:43,903 --> 00:14:45,277
So, what's our new plan?

344
00:14:45,361 --> 00:14:48,277
Our group battle plan
is what we expected,

345
00:14:48,361 --> 00:14:50,320
but we have another member now.

346
00:14:50,404 --> 00:14:51,113
Should we change strategies?

347
00:14:51,195 --> 00:14:53,195
We don't have much time.

348
00:14:53,278 --> 00:14:54,404
Bonito flakes.

349
00:14:54,487 --> 00:14:55,278
Well I think that'll
depend on Yuuji.

350
00:14:55,362 --> 00:14:57,946
What are your specialties?

351
00:14:58,029 --> 00:14:59,654
Punch, kick--

352
00:14:59,737 --> 00:15:02,237
We're already pretty
well set for all of that.

353
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:03,321
Huh?

354
00:15:04,238 --> 00:15:05,030
I don't know what
he's been doing,

355
00:15:05,114 --> 00:15:08,321
since he's been
dead for a while now.

356
00:15:08,405 --> 00:15:10,114
But I can say this much,

357
00:15:10,196 --> 00:15:12,279
if we all fought him
without cursed energy

358
00:15:13,905 --> 00:15:15,863
Itadori'd still beat us.

359
00:15:15,948 --> 00:15:16,948
[Both] Oh?

360
00:15:18,239 --> 00:15:20,697
Megumi's saying that,
even after fighting Toudou?

361
00:15:21,781 --> 00:15:23,322
That makes it pretty convincing.

362
00:15:23,406 --> 00:15:25,073
Interesting!

363
00:15:29,782 --> 00:15:30,698
"Kyoto Side Meeting"

364
00:15:30,782 --> 00:15:33,698
You must kill Yuuji Itadori!

365
00:15:33,782 --> 00:15:36,074
Sukuna's vessel is
not an actual person.

366
00:15:36,157 --> 00:15:38,365
So the act will go unquestioned.

367
00:15:38,448 --> 00:15:40,323
Without a doubt the entire event

368
00:15:40,407 --> 00:15:42,366
will be seen as an accident.

369
00:15:42,449 --> 00:15:45,282
So there's no need for
you to hold back or hesitate.

370
00:15:45,366 --> 00:15:46,533
I don't want to!

371
00:15:46,616 --> 00:15:48,324
You're telling us to kill him.

372
00:15:48,408 --> 00:15:52,324
But he's only here because
he didn't die the last time.

373
00:15:52,408 --> 00:15:54,866
I've been told that
Itadori's previous death

374
00:15:54,950 --> 00:15:56,534
was by suicide.

375
00:15:56,617 --> 00:15:57,534
Kamo?

376
00:15:57,617 --> 00:15:58,676
When ending a hostile sorcerer,

377
00:15:58,700 --> 00:16:01,492
what is the one thing you
must be cautious about?

378
00:16:02,283 --> 00:16:03,200
Sir.

379
00:16:03,283 --> 00:16:05,409
So that they don't
come back as a curse

380
00:16:05,492 --> 00:16:08,367
you must kill them
with cursed energy.

381
00:16:08,450 --> 00:16:09,535
Yes, correct.

382
00:16:09,618 --> 00:16:12,035
As long as one of you
delivers the finishing blow

383
00:16:12,119 --> 00:16:14,201
using cursed energy
all will be well.

384
00:16:14,284 --> 00:16:15,785
For now, Yuuji Itadori

385
00:16:15,868 --> 00:16:17,302
seems to have full
control over his body.

386
00:16:17,326 --> 00:16:19,743
So unless Sukuna comes out,

387
00:16:19,827 --> 00:16:21,743
the boy is just
another first-year.

388
00:16:21,827 --> 00:16:24,744
Which means that
killing him will be--

389
00:16:24,828 --> 00:16:25,744
This sucks!

390
00:16:25,828 --> 00:16:26,994
Do what you want.

391
00:16:27,078 --> 00:16:28,120
Hold on, Toudou.

392
00:16:28,202 --> 00:16:31,536
The principal
hasn't finished yet.

393
00:16:31,619 --> 00:16:33,911
Takada will be making
a live appearance

394
00:16:33,994 --> 00:16:36,203
on a TV show today at eleven.

395
00:16:36,286 --> 00:16:38,745
And I am not gonna miss that.

396
00:16:38,829 --> 00:16:39,954
You can record it.

397
00:16:40,037 --> 00:16:41,370
Come back.

398
00:16:41,453 --> 00:16:45,037
I'm gonna watch it in real
time and I'm gonna record it!

399
00:16:45,121 --> 00:16:46,662
What kinda fool
d'you think I am?

400
00:16:49,163 --> 00:16:49,579
That's what you're
worried about?

401
00:16:49,663 --> 00:16:51,830
You all listen up!

402
00:16:51,913 --> 00:16:53,163
And you too, old man!

403
00:16:53,913 --> 00:16:56,080
I've been putting up
with all of your failures

404
00:16:56,163 --> 00:16:58,621
and your lousy taste in
women for long enough!

405
00:16:58,704 --> 00:17:01,163
So you can plot and scheme
all you want on your own.

406
00:17:01,246 --> 00:17:04,414
But now, if you try to
order me around again,

407
00:17:04,497 --> 00:17:06,580
I will kill you!

408
00:17:11,039 --> 00:17:12,330
So what do we do now?

409
00:17:12,414 --> 00:17:14,580
How are we gonna
carry out the game plan

410
00:17:14,665 --> 00:17:16,998
with Toudou acting like that?

411
00:17:17,082 --> 00:17:19,040
Now the principal's
gone off too.

412
00:17:19,124 --> 00:17:21,224
Personally, I really don't
want to be killed by that guy.

413
00:17:21,248 --> 00:17:24,289
Does it even matter?

414
00:17:24,373 --> 00:17:25,206
Toudou's just going
to charge head-first

415
00:17:25,289 --> 00:17:28,041
into the Tokyo team anyway.

416
00:17:28,125 --> 00:17:29,666
So I figure while
he goes berserk

417
00:17:29,749 --> 00:17:31,874
the rest of us can
just keep our efforts

418
00:17:31,958 --> 00:17:33,374
focused on the game.

419
00:17:33,457 --> 00:17:37,290
Don't forget we have direct
orders to kill Yuuji Itadori.

420
00:17:37,374 --> 00:17:38,392
We're seriously doing this?

421
00:17:38,416 --> 00:17:42,667
Honestly, I doubt Toudou
will actually kill him.

422
00:17:42,750 --> 00:17:44,542
But he is capable of it.

423
00:17:44,625 --> 00:17:46,126
Then we'll need
to assign someone

424
00:17:46,208 --> 00:17:47,458
to keep an eye on Toudou,

425
00:17:47,542 --> 00:17:49,262
and deliver the final
blow to Yuuji Itadori.

426
00:17:51,208 --> 00:17:52,458
I don't like this.

427
00:17:52,542 --> 00:17:56,501
Because of the cursed spirits
we'll all be in two-man cells.

428
00:17:56,584 --> 00:17:58,626
So that works for us.

429
00:17:58,709 --> 00:17:59,709
No.

430
00:18:00,292 --> 00:18:02,835
Allowing a half-wit
like Yuuji Itadori

431
00:18:02,918 --> 00:18:07,043
to exist as a sorcerer at this
school is a serious problem.

432
00:18:07,127 --> 00:18:09,419
One that goes beyond this event.

433
00:18:09,502 --> 00:18:12,086
As Kamo clan elder I decree,

434
00:18:13,002 --> 00:18:14,544
it must end.

435
00:18:14,627 --> 00:18:16,961
We will all attack
Itadori together.

436
00:18:17,961 --> 00:18:19,293
Hold on.

437
00:18:19,377 --> 00:18:22,545
What if Toge Inumaki is there
with Itadori when we attack?

438
00:18:22,628 --> 00:18:25,920
Having all of us in one
place is a risky move

439
00:18:26,003 --> 00:18:28,045
with that cursed speech user.

440
00:18:28,129 --> 00:18:31,545
Worst case, he could
wipe us all out at once.

441
00:18:31,628 --> 00:18:33,711
She has a point.

442
00:18:33,796 --> 00:18:35,004
No.

443
00:18:35,088 --> 00:18:37,504
If you know he's coming,
he's not that difficult to handle.

444
00:18:37,587 --> 00:18:41,046
Let me take care of
Maki and while I'm at it

445
00:18:41,130 --> 00:18:43,046
that brown-haired
first year as well.

446
00:18:43,130 --> 00:18:44,337
What's on your mind?

447
00:18:44,421 --> 00:18:46,379
You're starting to
sound like Toudou.

448
00:18:46,462 --> 00:18:49,089
(growl)

449
00:18:49,172 --> 00:18:49,588
Well then?

450
00:18:49,672 --> 00:18:51,964
What did you want?

451
00:18:52,047 --> 00:18:52,964
Huh?

452
00:18:53,047 --> 00:18:54,588
Are you upset now?

453
00:18:54,672 --> 00:18:56,922
No I'm not upset at all.

454
00:18:57,005 --> 00:18:58,213
'Course not.

455
00:18:58,296 --> 00:18:59,736
'Cause I haven't
done anything wrong.

456
00:18:59,797 --> 00:19:00,548
(irritated growl)

457
00:19:00,631 --> 00:19:03,173
But I'm afraid we have a spy.

458
00:19:04,048 --> 00:19:05,464
Someone's working with a curse

459
00:19:05,548 --> 00:19:07,756
-or a curse user here.
-(gasp)

460
00:19:07,840 --> 00:19:09,090
Impossible!

461
00:19:09,173 --> 00:19:10,357
A curse user's one thing,
but working with curses?

462
00:19:10,381 --> 00:19:12,548
And yet a lot of
them on that level

463
00:19:12,631 --> 00:19:15,715
have been popping up lately.

464
00:19:15,799 --> 00:19:16,959
They understand human speech,

465
00:19:17,007 --> 00:19:20,133
and they've formed a faction
that's operating with purpose.

466
00:19:20,215 --> 00:19:21,525
They might think
they're just working

467
00:19:21,549 --> 00:19:23,424
with a curse user, but...

468
00:19:23,507 --> 00:19:26,340
You need to investigate
everyone at Kyoto.

469
00:19:28,716 --> 00:19:31,800
For all you know I could
be the traitor so why me?

470
00:19:31,883 --> 00:19:32,800
Ohh no way!

471
00:19:32,883 --> 00:19:34,175
You're too weak.

472
00:19:34,258 --> 00:19:35,842
You don't have
the guts for that.

473
00:19:37,425 --> 00:19:40,801
Ooh! Hysterics are a
turnoff for men, you know.

474
00:19:40,884 --> 00:19:41,801
[Utahime] That's enough!

475
00:19:41,884 --> 00:19:43,342
I'm the senior in charge here!

476
00:19:48,342 --> 00:19:48,509
[Megumi] Itadori.

477
00:19:48,592 --> 00:19:50,551
Hmm?

478
00:19:50,634 --> 00:19:51,968
You okay?

479
00:19:52,051 --> 00:19:55,593
Yeah, but I've got a
big job, from what I hear.

480
00:19:55,677 --> 00:19:58,760
I mean about what happened.

481
00:19:58,844 --> 00:20:00,635
Ha, no, nothing happened!

482
00:20:03,844 --> 00:20:04,844
'Kay, yeah.

483
00:20:06,511 --> 00:20:07,928
Something did happen.

484
00:20:08,011 --> 00:20:09,131
But it's true that I'm okay.

485
00:20:10,928 --> 00:20:14,302
In fact, because of it I
really don't want to lose.

486
00:20:15,886 --> 00:20:16,803
Alright then.

487
00:20:16,886 --> 00:20:18,053
Huh?

488
00:20:18,137 --> 00:20:20,595
Because I don't
wanna lose either.

489
00:20:20,679 --> 00:20:22,470
Why're you two
talking about losing?

490
00:20:22,554 --> 00:20:24,012
After you already
got rolled once!

491
00:20:24,096 --> 00:20:25,679
Whoa! Let's go!

492
00:20:25,762 --> 00:20:26,846
Let's kick their asses!

493
00:20:26,929 --> 00:20:28,554
Let's do it for Maki!

494
00:20:28,637 --> 00:20:29,387
Don't say stuff like that.

495
00:20:29,470 --> 00:20:30,512
Pollack roe.

496
00:20:30,595 --> 00:20:32,596
Yeah! Let's do it for Maki!

497
00:20:32,680 --> 00:20:34,513
[Maki] I said, don't
say stuff like that!

498
00:20:37,680 --> 00:20:39,805
In that case...

499
00:20:39,888 --> 00:20:40,888
Let's win!

500
00:20:41,638 --> 00:20:42,555
(grunt)

501
00:20:42,638 --> 00:20:44,221
Who said you could go first?

502
00:20:44,721 --> 00:20:48,472
(ending theme music)

503
00:22:16,395 --> 00:22:17,980
Juju Stroll!

504
00:22:18,063 --> 00:22:19,188
"Sushi Eishuu"

505
00:22:21,271 --> 00:22:22,438
Hi!

506
00:22:22,521 --> 00:22:23,831
Today we're at the
famous sushi restaurant

507
00:22:23,855 --> 00:22:25,563
known as Sushi Eishuu!

508
00:22:26,729 --> 00:22:29,604
You should dress
like that and be on TV.

509
00:22:29,688 --> 00:22:32,439
You know you'd be
mad at me if I did that.

510
00:22:34,230 --> 00:22:36,148
[Sushi Chef] Welcome
to Sushi Eishuu.

511
00:22:47,773 --> 00:22:48,606
So what would you like, Takada?

512
00:22:48,690 --> 00:22:49,606
What's your favorite?

513
00:22:49,690 --> 00:22:51,940
I really love goatfish!

514
00:22:52,023 --> 00:22:52,606
And room-temperature sake!

515
00:22:52,690 --> 00:22:54,565
They go great together!

516
00:22:54,648 --> 00:22:57,023
Uhh, just how old are you?

517
00:22:57,107 --> 00:22:58,108
Huh?

518
00:23:02,357 --> 00:23:04,482
How long have you
been making sushi, boss?

519
00:23:05,566 --> 00:23:06,816
Since I was 20 years old.

520
00:23:06,899 --> 00:23:10,984
Which I guess probably
means about 300 years?

521
00:23:11,900 --> 00:23:12,817
Are you drunk?

522
00:23:12,900 --> 00:23:15,733
[Sushi Chef] Here.
Enjoy your goatfish.

523
00:23:16,442 --> 00:23:17,859
Mmm!

524
00:23:17,942 --> 00:23:18,942
Ohhh, mmm!

525
00:23:20,275 --> 00:23:21,275
That is so good!

526
00:23:22,567 --> 00:23:24,193
